// trace(): software ray queries for every non-primary visibility and lighting caller
// (render v3, council-v3 architecture D1; ara_render look::trace, ara_bvh). A
// threaded binary TLAS over instances and one compressed eight-wide BVH (CWBVH,
// Ylitie et al. 2017) per mesh with precomputed triangles (Baldwin and Weber 2016):
// the R4-1/R5-6 tuned kernel's data and traversal, plus world transforms, t ranges,
// ray flags, instance masks, face culling and alpha tests. No hardware RT, no
// stochastic choice: the same ray always gives the same hit.
// Include after raster.slangh (bindless buffers[], textures[], samplers[]).
//
// Hardware backend seam (not built; hardware RT stays an optional backend, off by
// default): a TRACE_HARDWARE build would implement traceClosestWith/traceAnyWith with
// RayQuery over a TLAS whose instance custom index is the trace instance slot and
// whose BLASes index triangles in source order, call the same ITraceAlpha on
// non-opaque candidates and fill the same TraceHit; callers do not change.
//
// The CWBVH traversal (traceBlas, traceChildren) is ported from tinybvh
// (tiny_bvh_base.h at c9be3103cc9693b456b0a0353927c11cac7d710f, BVH8_CWBVH::Intersect,
// via the R4-1 tuned WGSL kernel); Ara adds world transforms, t ranges, flags,
// masks, face culling, alpha tests, edge slack and 128-bit loads.
//
